# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/fusion-2 window (the prefill levers on the ship stack: the prefill SDPA with one q chunk per core, WPP, and the 13x10 matmul grids, M1; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/fusion-2 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job). Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-6 is the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (the oneq lever needs its binary; every arm without the flag runs that binary with the lever off). A commit of a file the image
# carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# PL2 (TIMED, the COMBINED prefill ABAB, repeat pair): the LEVERS again (B2), UNPROFILED, with C2_TELEMETRY=1. prefill_ladder_solo: four real-code prompts of about 4,096 /
# 32,768 / 131,072 / 253,920 tokens, ONE request at a time with nothing else running, a 16-token answer: the time to first token and the prefill rate of each rung. Every
# boot a fresh reset, one tag at a time. TIMED: the ARC runner sets are at ZERO for this job (ORDER.txt, ARC-ZERO); no build, no CI push, no other job beside it. READ:
# c2_smoke_check clean (a lever boot also has its engaged lines and no fell-back line; a control boot has none of the lever's lines), no stall; then python3 -B
# scripts/ci/prefill_ladder_report.py <control results> --second <lever results> for the pairs (PC1, PL1) and (PC2, PL2): the TTFT of the lever over the control per rung (a
# ratio below 1 is faster), the prefill rate, and the answer text of every rung equal between the arms (greedy text cannot depend on the prefill grid or the SDPA core
# layout). The control-to-control spread (PC1 against PC2) is the floor a gain has to beat. TELEMETRY (C2_TELEMETRY=1, scripts/ci/card_telemetry.py): the read-only ARC
# sidecar samples every chip once a second through the smoke step (AICLK and the limiter holding it, power, current, temperature); read
# telemetry-smoke/telemetry-summary.txt beside the result, and the first [TELEMETRY] line must say decode check ok. It runs on the host and is not part of any arm; it is on
# every leg so the pairs stay paired. A gain that comes with a different loaded AICLK between the arms is the clocks, not the lever. Duration (estimate): boot 10 minutes,
# the solo ladder 5 (about 66 to 98 s for the 254k rung), 25 minutes in all; the box is 60.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-6
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-all-oneq-grid13
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,prefill_ladder_solo
C2_SMOKE_PARTIAL=solo prefill ladder: the protocol fixes its test list, so concurrent8_steady is not run
C2_TELEMETRY=1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=60
